## Caching

Next.js uses a caching strategy that handles both static and dynamic routes. The default caching is:

- **`force-dynamic`** — the page is always dynamic
- **`no-store`** — the page is always dynamic
- **`revalidate`** — the page is revalidated at most once per request

If a page with `revalidate` has the same cache strategy as a route, Next.js will serve the cached version for maximum cache hit rate.

> **Good to know**:
>
> - By default, `cache` is set to `no-store`.
> - You can also set `cache: 'no-store'` if you want to disable caching for all pages.
> - Next.js will _not_ cache a dynamic route. See [Dynamic Routing](/docs/app/api-reference/file-conventions/dynamic-routes) for more details.

